<opml version="2.0">
  <head>
    <title>JLR Environmental Consulting - Comprehensive Signals of Change Listening Post</title>
    <dateCreated>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:30:00 -0700</dateCreated>
    <ownerName>JLR Environmental Consulting / Economic Gardening</ownerName>
    <docs>https://opml.org/spec2.opml</docs>
  </head>
  <body>
    <outline text="00 - START HERE / HOW THIS LISTENING POST IS ORGANIZED" title="00 - START HERE / HOW THIS LISTENING POST IS ORGANIZED" description="Organized around JLR Questions 1-5 and the Economic Gardening Signals of Change approach.">
      <outline text="Q1: Where is the opportunity? Market, funding, regulatory and project-demand signals." title="Q1: Where is the opportunity? Market, funding, regulatory and project-demand signals." type="note" />
      <outline text="Q2: Who should we pursue? Existing clients plus Priority A/B/C target organizations." title="Q2: Who should we pursue? Existing clients plus Priority A/B/C target organizations." type="note" />
      <outline text="Q3: What is happening there now? Signals of change, projects, failures, funding, plans and procurements." title="Q3: What is happening there now? Signals of change, projects, failures, funding, plans and procurements." type="note" />
      <outline text="Q4: Who do we need to know? Leadership, engineering, project and procurement changes." title="Q4: Who do we need to know? Leadership, engineering, project and procurement changes." type="note" />
      <outline text="Q5: How and when can we compete? RFQ/RFP/SOQ, on-call/MSA, prequalification, awards and contract timing." title="Q5: How and when can we compete? RFQ/RFP/SOQ, on-call/MSA, prequalification, awards and contract timing." type="note" />
      <outline text="IMPORTANT: Procurement portals vary. Some require vendor registration/login or do not provide public APIs/RSS. The feeds below monitor public pages and search-indexed notices; some portals will still require manual/vendor-alert monitoring." title="IMPORTANT: Procurement portals vary. Some require vendor registration/login or do not provide public APIs/RSS. The feeds below monitor public pages and search-indexed notices; some portals will still require manual/vendor-alert monitoring." type="note" />
      <outline text="Competitor/prime feeds are for market intelligence: wins, funding, client relationships, on-call awards, teaming and project activity." title="Competitor/prime feeds are for market intelligence: wins, funding, client relationships, on-call awards, teaming and project activity." type="note" />
      <outline text="Feed queries are intentionally signal-focused to reduce noise. FeedMe can deduplicate overlapping hits." title="Feed queries are intentionally signal-focused to reduce noise. FeedMe can deduplicate overlapping hits." type="note" />
    <outline text="v2 (Sep 2026): Folders 04-08 entity queries tightened (dropped generic single-word OR terms like 'contract'/'construction'/'funding' that were causing unrelated articles to match; kept specific multi-word phrases and added leadership terms)." title="v2 (Sep 2026): Folders 04-08 entity queries tightened (dropped generic single-word OR terms like 'contract'/'construction'/'funding' that were causing unrelated articles to match; kept specific multi-word phrases and added leadership terms)." type="note" /><outline text="v2: Folder 13 trade-press feeds swapped from Bing search-wrapper URLs to verified native publisher RSS (Maven's Notebook, ENR California + Water &amp; Dams, ACWA, CWEA, Water Finance &amp; Management, Construction Dive) for cleaner, higher-precision signal." title="v2: Folder 13 trade-press feeds swapped from Bing search-wrapper URLs to verified native publisher RSS (Maven's Notebook, ENR California + Water &amp; Dams, ACWA, CWEA, Water Finance &amp; Management, Construction Dive) for cleaner, higher-precision signal." type="note" /><outline text="v2: Folder 03 gained 6 feeds scoped to the actual procurement-portal instance used by each of the 6 Existing Clients found to use Public Purchase/OpenGov, instead of relying only on statewide portal searches." title="v2: Folder 03 gained 6 feeds scoped to the actual procurement-portal instance used by each of the 6 Existing Clients found to use Public Purchase/OpenGov, instead of relying only on statewide portal searches." type="note" /><outline text="v2: No public RSS exists for most small agencies' own bid/RFP pages or for Public Purchase/OpenGov/PlanetBids/DemandStar/Cal eProcure vendor notifications (registration/login required) -- see JLR_Existing_Clients_Bid_Pages_Reference.docx for direct manual-check links." title="v2: No public RSS exists for most small agencies' own bid/RFP pages or for Public Purchase/OpenGov/PlanetBids/DemandStar/Cal eProcure vendor notifications (registration/login required) -- see JLR_Existing_Clients_Bid_Pages_Reference.docx for direct manual-check links." type="note" /><outline text="v3 (Sep 2026): Removed 6 dead-weight feeds -- Grants.gov Modified Opportunities (nationwide, all-category noise) x2, SAM.gov and Cal eProcure CA Water/Engineering (wrong procurement platforms for local agency work), Legistar Engineering Awards (statewide unscoped, too generic), Industrial Pump Manufacturing California (not a verifiable real entity)." title="v3 (Sep 2026): Removed 6 dead-weight feeds -- Grants.gov Modified Opportunities (nationwide, all-category noise) x2, SAM.gov and Cal eProcure CA Water/Engineering (wrong procurement platforms for local agency work), Legistar Engineering Awards (statewide unscoped, too generic), Industrial Pump Manufacturing California (not a verifiable real entity)." type="note" /><outline text="v3: Rebuilt 8 folder-09 partner-ecosystem queries that were quoting a padded phrase (e.g. 'Affinity Engineering California') instead of the real company name, which meant they almost never matched real article text -- now quote the verified legal/trade name only, with topic terms in a separate OR-clause (matches Domenichelli &amp; Associates / Larsen Wurzel &amp; Associates pattern). '510 LR Development California' was left as-is -- could not verify a real matching entity; confirm the intended company name." title="v3: Rebuilt 8 folder-09 partner-ecosystem queries that were quoting a padded phrase (e.g. 'Affinity Engineering California') instead of the real company name, which meant they almost never matched real article text -- now quote the verified legal/trade name only, with topic terms in a separate OR-clause (matches Domenichelli &amp; Associates / Larsen Wurzel &amp; Associates pattern). '510 LR Development California' was left as-is -- could not verify a real matching entity; confirm the intended company name." type="note" /><outline text="v4 (Sep 2026): Removed the 6 bare Public Purchase/OpenGov portal-scoped feeds added in v2 (West Sacramento, Roseville, Olivehurst PUD, South Tahoe PUD, San Juan WD, Placer County Water Agency). These used a site: restriction with no topical/geographic keyword pairing, and the underlying portal pages are login-gated with no crawlable public content -- Bing's search-as-RSS wrapper returned zero real hits every run and degraded to unrelated filler (e.g. Chattanooga, TN tourism/city pages) that cost AI-analysis spend for zero signal. Manually check these 6 portals directly per JLR_Existing_Clients_Bid_Pages_Reference.docx instead." title="v4 (Sep 2026): Removed the 6 bare Public Purchase/OpenGov portal-scoped feeds added in v2 (West Sacramento, Roseville, Olivehurst PUD, South Tahoe PUD, San Juan WD, Placer County Water Agency). These used a site: restriction with no topical/geographic keyword pairing, and the underlying portal pages are login-gated with no crawlable public content -- Bing's search-as-RSS wrapper returned zero real hits every run and degraded to unrelated filler (e.g. Chattanooga, TN tourism/city pages) that cost AI-analysis spend for zero signal. Manually check these 6 portals directly per JLR_Existing_Clients_Bid_Pages_Reference.docx instead." type="note" /></outline>
    <outline text="01 - OFFICIAL GOVERNMENT / REGULATORY SOURCES" title="01 - OFFICIAL GOVERNMENT / REGULATORY SOURCES" description="Primary government sources for funding, rules, programs, grants, compliance and public infrastructure activity.">
      <outline text="Grants.gov - New Opportunities by Agency" title="Grants.gov - New Opportunities by Agency" type="rss" xmlUrl="https://www.grants.gov/rss/GG_NewOppByAgency.xml" htmlUrl="https://www.grants.gov/connect/rss-feeds" description="Official Grants.gov RSS feed." sourceType="Direct RSS" />
      <outline text="Grants.gov - New Opportunities by Category" title="Grants.gov - New Opportunities by Category" type="rss" xmlUrl="https://www.grants.gov/rss/GG_NewOppByCategory.xml" htmlUrl="https://www.grants.gov/connect/rss-feeds" description="Official Grants.gov RSS feed." sourceType="Direct RSS" />
      </outline>
    <outline text="02 - FUNDING / FINANCIAL COMMITMENT SIGNALS" title="02 - FUNDING / FINANCIAL COMMITMENT SIGNALS" description="Signals that convert plans into more actionable projects.">
